 "title": "Elections - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota",
 "text": "Elections - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nSkip to content\nOctober 18, 2026\nOglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nHome\nOnline Map\nAbout\nDirectory »\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nClerk of Court\nPublic Health Nurse\nDirector of Equalization\nEmergency Management\nGIS\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nState’s Attorney\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service Officer\nWeed & Pest\nCommission »\nCounty Commissioners\n2026 Minute Archive\n2025 Minute Archive\n2024 Minute Archive\nOlder Minute Archive\nEmployment (2)\nQuick Links\nFall River Co.\nElections\n2026 General Election Information\nEarly Voting\nEarly Voting for the General Election begins September 17th, 2026 at the Fall River County Courthouse in Hot Springs and at the Sacred Heart Church Hall, 30238 US Hwy 18, Pine Ridge and will end November 2nd, 2026.\nRegistration Deadline\nThe deadline to register for the 2026 General Election is October 19th, 2026.\nElection date\nThe General Election is on November 3rd, 2026.\nSample Ballot\nSample ballots are available to voters through the state Voter Information Portal .\nMaps\nCommissioner District Map\nOglala Lakota Precinct Map\nPine Ridge 1 & Pine Ridge 3 area precinct map\nPolling Places\nBatesland : Oglala Lakota County Schools – Bill Conquering Bear Gymnasium – 409 3rd St, Batesland\nCuny Table : Red Shirt School – 38 Tatanka Numpa Rd, Redshirt\nKyle : Little Wound School – 438 Main St, Kyle\nManderson: Wounded Knee Business Office, 14 Manderson School Rd, Manderson\nOglala : Brother Renee Hall – 29126 US Hwy 18, Oglala\nPine Ridge 1 & 3: Sacred Heart Church Hall , 30238 US Hwy 18, Pine Ridge\nPorcupine : Christ the King Parish – Bill Pauly Hall – 490 Lourdes Ln, Porcupine\nRockyford: Wakan Tiopspa #12 Community Building – 112 Steele Place, Porcupine\nAbsentee Voting\nVoter Registration\nVoter Identification\nElection Results\nHere is a link to the South Dakota Secretary of States website\nVoters may obtain voting information through the Secretary of State’s website by accessing the Voter Information Portal. There, you may view your voter registration, polling place and sample ballots. If you are voting by absentee ballot, you may also track the date your absentee ballot request was received, the date your ballot was mailed and the date your completed ballot was received by the Auditor’s Office. You may access this information at the following link: Voter Information Portal\nContact Information:\nelection@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\n605-745-5130\nReturn to Auditor’s Page\nQuick Links\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nAbsentee Voting\nElections\nVoter Registration\nVoter Identification\nSD State Election Resources\nSD State Voter Portal\n2026 Summer Reassessment\nNational Active Fires Map\nWebsite Survey\nWebsite Survey\nPlease let us know about your visit to our site.\nWhere did you hear about this website? * Search Engine Friend Other\nWhat were your reasons for looking at our site? *\nGeneral Information\nSpecific Information\nCuriosity\nOther\nDid you find what you were looking for? *\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nIf no, what information were you looking for? (Please be specific so that we can improve our website.) *\nIf you would like a response to your request for additional information please list your email below.\nSubmit\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in\nNotifications",
